I found that if I manually split - apply - combine I can get the desired result:

persons <- split(df, f = df$pers.id <http://pers.id>)
persons <- lapply(persons, na.omit)
persons <- persons[sapply(persons, function(x) all(is.na <http://is.na>(x))==FALSE)]
persons <- lapply(persons, FUN=function(x) dcast(x, pers.id <http://pers.id> ~ variable))
dd <- rbind.fill(persons)
dd == required

What puzzles me is 'dcast(df, pers.id <http://pers.id> ~ variable)' works straight away with the example data as you have demonstrated but not with my real life data. I have checked the structure and tehr are no missing values in the 'value' column.

I would still be interested to understand this issue even though there is a workaround

